---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { BLANKET_SIZES, QUILT_SIZES, MATTRESS_SIZES } from '../../lib/reference/sizes';
import { siteConfig, CANONICAL_PERSON_ID } from '../../config/site';

const title = 'Blanket, Quilt & Mattress Sizes';
const description =
  'Reference chart of common blanket, quilt, and US mattress sizes in inches for fiber arts planning. Scrollable tables for phones.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'CollectionPage',
      name: title,
      description,
      url: `${siteConfig.siteUrl}/reference/quilt-sizes/`,
      author: { '@id': CANONICAL_PERSON_ID },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${siteConfig.siteUrl}/` },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Reference', item: `${siteConfig.siteUrl}/reference/` },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Sizes', item: `${siteConfig.siteUrl}/reference/quilt-sizes/` },
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/reference/quilt-sizes/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="container prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Reference', href: '/reference/' }, { label: 'Sizes' }]} />
    <h1>Standard blanket, quilt &amp; mattress sizes</h1>
    <div class="takeaway">
      <p><strong>Key takeaway:</strong> A common US queen mattress is about 60×80 inches; quilt and knit/crochet blanket sizes are craft conventions that vary by pattern. Use these tables as starting points in the <a href="/tools/quilt-size-calculator/">quilt size</a> and <a href="/tools/yarn-blanket-calculator/">yarn blanket</a> calculators.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="meta-row"><span>Last reviewed {siteConfig.lastReviewed}</span></p>
    <p>
      These tables are planning aids. Knit/crochet blanket and quilt-top sizes are craft conventions that vary by
      pattern. Mattress sizes below are common US <em>retail rounded</em> dimensions; industry finished-mattress
      specs (ISPA) are often about ½″ shorter and list full/double finished width as 53″ rather than the 54″ retail
      figure many shops quote. Always confirm your pattern and your mattress before cutting.
    </p>

    <h2>Knit / crochet blanket sizes (inches)</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Blanket sizes table">
      <table>
        <caption>Common knit and crochet blanket finished sizes</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Width</th><th>Length</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {BLANKET_SIZES.map((s) => <tr><td>{s.name}</td><td>{s.widthIn}</td><td>{s.lengthIn}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Common quilt top sizes (inches)</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Quilt sizes table">
      <table>
        <caption>Common quilt top finished sizes</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Width</th><th>Length</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {QUILT_SIZES.map((s) => <tr><td>{s.name}</td><td>{s.widthIn}</td><td>{s.lengthIn}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>US mattress sizes (inches)</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Mattress sizes table">
      <table>
        <caption>Common US retail mattress dimensions (rounded)</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Width</th><th>Length</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {MATTRESS_SIZES.map((s) => <tr><td>{s.name}</td><td>{s.widthIn}</td><td>{s.lengthIn}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>How to use these sizes with FiberCalc tools</h2>
    <p>
      Pick a target top size (or mattress plus desired drop), then use the
      <a href="/tools/quilt-size-calculator/">quilt size calculator</a> to fit blocks, sashing, and borders. Add
      overhang in the <a href="/tools/quilt-backing-calculator/">backing calculator</a> (default 4″ per side for
      longarm prep). Convert the finished perimeter into binding strips with the
      <a href="/tools/quilt-binding-calculator/">binding calculator</a>. Knit/crochet makers estimating yarn for a
      throw-sized blanket can enter the blanket table dimensions in the
      <a href="/tools/yarn-blanket-calculator/">yarn blanket calculator</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Worked example: queen bed quilt</h2>
    <p>
      A common US queen mattress is about 60×80″. A quilt top near 84×92″ leaves roughly 12″ of total side drop and
      12″ of foot drop before accounting for mattress height and tuck—adjust for your bed and preference. Backing for
      an 84×92″ top with 4″ overhang needs about 92×100″ of fabric coverage before panel seams; binding uses
      perimeter 2 × (84 + 92) = 352″ plus join waste.
    </p>

    <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Buying fabric for the mattress size instead of the finished quilt top plus overhang.</li>
      <li>Treating knit “throw” and quilt “throw” labels as identical inch measurements—they often differ.</li>
      <li>Ignoring pillow tuck or mattress depth when planning drop.</li>
      <li>Assuming ISPA finished specs and retail labels always match to the inch (especially full/double width).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        US mattress dimensions as commonly published in bedding retail charts; industry context via the
        <a href="https://www.sleepproducts.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">International Sleep Products Association</a>
        (checked {siteConfig.lastReviewed}). Retail rounded sizes shown here may differ slightly from ISPA finished
        mattress specs.
      </li>
      <li>Quilt and craft blanket ranges reflect widespread pattern conventions; always confirm your pattern.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Related tools and guides:
      <a href="/tools/quilt-size-calculator/">quilt size calculator</a>,
      <a href="/tools/quilt-backing-calculator/">backing calculator</a>,
      <a href="/tools/quilt-binding-calculator/">binding calculator</a>,
      <a href="/guides/quilt-backing-yardage-guide/">backing yardage guide</a>,
      <a href="/guides/how-much-quilt-binding-do-i-need/">binding guide</a>,
      <a href="/quilting/">quilting hub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
